---
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
import Legal from '../components/Legal.astro'
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro'
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
---

<Base
  title="Terms · Matra"
  description="Plain terms for the hosted account and paid packages. The framework is MIT and these terms do not touch it."
>
  <Nav />
  <Legal
    kicker="Terms"
    title="Plain terms.<br />No lock-in."
    lede="These cover the account and anything you pay us for · not the MIT core, which its own licence already covers."
    updated="24 August 2026"
  >
    <h2>Using Matra</h2>
    <p>
      <code>@matrajs/core</code> and the framework bindings are MIT. Nothing here takes that back,
      and nothing here applies to code you ship with them.
    </p>
    <p>An account is for one organisation. Sharing credentials outside it will close it.</p>

    <h2>Paying</h2>
    <p>
      Subscriptions renew until cancelled, and cancelling stops the next charge rather than the
      current period. Ask within 14 days of a charge and we refund it, without asking why.
    </p>
    <p>
      Plans are capped by the number of developers writing code against the paid packages.
      Adding one inside your cap costs nothing and needs no paperwork.
    </p>

    <h2>What we promise</h2>
    <p>
      The service is provided as it is. We will tell you before a breaking change to a paid
      feature. We will not hold your documents hostage if you leave · export is a button rather
      than a support ticket.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>A lapsed subscription cannot switch anything off.</strong> Nothing checks a licence
      at runtime and nothing contacts us, so software you already shipped keeps running whatever happens
      to your billing.
    </p>

    <h2>What we ask</h2>
    <p>
      Do not resell the hosted service as your own, and do not use it to store anything illegal.
      That is the whole list.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes and law</h2>
    <p>
      Changes are posted here with a new date. These terms are governed by the laws of
      Bangladesh. Questions: <strong>legal@amrela.co</strong>.
    </p>
  </Legal>
  <Footer />
</Base>
